 R←Test_Open_088(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;parms;json;qdmx;threw;success;log
⍝ When the "lx" function of a project crashes, the report must name the error that occurred, rather
⍝ than just saying that one did.\\
⍝ `HandleLX` used to overwrite the message `ExecUnderTrap` had produced with its own headline, and
⍝ then built the detail out of the overwritten value - so the user was told that something had gone
⍝ wrong, was shown the headline spelled out one character per line, and never learned what the error
⍝ actually was.\\
⍝ Batch mode makes this deterministic: `HandleLX` then executes "lx" without asking, and throws.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 tempDir←∆GetFolderInTempDir⊃⎕SI
 #.⎕SHADOW'TEMP' ⋄ 'TEMP'#.⎕NS''
 tempDir ⎕NCOPY⍠('Wildcard' 1)⊣##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/LxProject/*'

⍝ A "lx" function that fails for a reason we can recognise again in the message. `⎕SIGNAL` rather
⍝ than an expression that merely ought to fail: it cannot be defused by whatever system variables
⍝ the project brings with it.\\
⍝ `⎕NPUT`'s left argument is (content [encoding] [nl]), so the lines must be enclosed
 (⊂' r←CrashOnPurpose' ' ⎕SIGNAL 11')⎕NPUT(tempDir,'/APLSource/DateAndTime/CrashOnPurpose.aplf')1
 json←⊃⎕NGET tempDir,'/apl-package.json'
 json←'lx: "Init"'⎕R'lx: "CrashOnPurpose"'⊢json
 (⊂json)⎕NPUT(tempDir,'/apl-package.json')1

 parms←##.Cider.CreateOpenParms ⍬
 parms.folder←tempDir
 parms.parent←'#.TEMP'
 parms.batch←1
 parms.ignoreUserExec←1

 threw←0
 :Trap 0
     (success log)←##.Cider.OpenProject parms
 :Else
     threw←1
     qdmx←⎕DMX
 :EndTrap
 →T.GoToTidyUp~threw

⍝ The headline and the return code, but above all the error itself
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'Executing "lx"'⍷qdmx.EM
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'RC=11'⍷qdmx.EM
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'DOMAIN ERROR'⍷qdmx.EM
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'CrashOnPurpose'⍷qdmx.EM

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 {}##.Cider.CloseProject'#.TEMP.DateAndTime'
 {}⎕SE.Link.Break'#.TEMP.DateAndTime'
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir,'/..'
⍝Done
